   00601|     // `data/seed/handler-rules.lino` and
   00602|     // `data/seed/multilingual-responses-policy.lino` introduced when eleven
   00603|     // handlers stopped being Rust -- the rule vocabulary (`agent_info`,
   00604|     // `backticks`, `cleaned`, `raw`, `literal`, `prompt`, `forms`), the
   00605|     // handler names themselves, and the response ids of their four-language
   00606|     // wording. Behaviour moving from Rust into seed data arrives as generated
   00607|     // closure records, which is what this floor is for. Four more followed when
   00608|     // those responses were given their Spanish text, which every supported
   00609|     // locale owes the others. Ten more arrived the same way with issues #1095
   00610|     // and #1099: two seed roles (`agentic_continuation_cue`,
   00611|     // `enumeration_cue`), the `agentic_continuation` handler and its
   00612|     // `continuation_cue` rule, that handler's five-language wording, and the
